\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There is no sorrow, Lord, too light
\par To bring in prayer to Thee;
\par Nor is there any care too slight
\par To wake Thy sympathy.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou who hast trod the thorny road
\par Wilt share each small distress;
\par The love which bore the greater load
\par Will not refuse the less.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There is no secret sigh we breathe
\par But meets the ear divine;
\par And every cross grows light beneath
\par The shadow, Lord, of Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Life's ills without, sin's strife within:
\par The heart would overflow,
\par But for that love which died for sin,
\par That love which wept with love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

